! Dangerous

<<~ ahu #/definition>>

!! Definition

A canonical risk hook: the Power forces a ''Danger Roll'' on activation regardless of skill or Level — d20 + ability + skill vs P, natural 1 always fails, failure runs the Corruption procedure.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/activation>>

!! Activation

''Modifies the activation protocol itself'', not the effect — it sits structurally above capability components. Where most components answer "what does it do," `dangerous` answers "what does pulling it risk."

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/interaction>>

!! Interaction

Composes with any domain or function. ''Vertical-vs-flat pressure lives here:'' the flat `#has` model treats `dangerous` as a peer of `ecm-scan`, but it modifies the crossing event, not the capability. Held flat on purpose (Principle); Sprint 4 tests whether flatness loses signal.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/filters>>

!! Filters

```text
[tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/sdm/components/hook/dangerous]]                 all dangerous modules — the vertical cross-section
